Hmmm, don't know if it works, but a random suggestion you can try:
In the plugin where it selects the file to load (const bit), put conditionals if the constuctor name is Scene_Status, check who the menuActor is and change the filename depending on that.
EDIT:
I tested it quickly and it seems to work if you replace the below
const bit = _.loadImage(_.backgrounds[this._menuBackgroundConstructorName]);
with (change the file names to what you want and add all actor ids)
let bit = 0;
if (this._menuBackgroundConstructorName == "Scene_Status") {
if ($gameParty._menuActorId == 2) {
bit = _.loadImage("Sword");
}
if ($gameParty._menuActorId == 1) {
bit = _.loadImage("Night");
}
} else {
bit = _.loadImage(_.backgrounds[this._menuBackgroundConstructorName]);
}
But yeah, there might be some problem that I'm unaware of and maybe you should add stuff to what it loads automatically(?). Ask some coders LOL.

